course: dictionary
lesson: 4214
title: Short words, long meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A short word can stand for a long one. GP is short for general practitioner. Writers shorten long names so they are quicker to read and easier to say.
explain: In «In the UK your first stop for most health problems is the GP, the general practitioner or family doctor», the words after GP tell you what it means. Look for clues like a comma, the word or, or words that explain the short form.
explain: Use the context to check your guess. Does your meaning fit? A GP is a doctor, so «see your GP» means see your family doctor. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to test it.
explain: Be careful with words that look alike. GPS is a different thing from GP. In «GPS measures the movement every day», GPS is a satellite system that finds places. Read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: GP stands for general practitioner.
fact: A GP is a family doctor who sees people for all kinds of illness at a local surgery or clinic.
fact: If you need a specialist, your GP can send you to one.
fact: GP can also stand for Grand Prix, a big motor race.
fact: For an emergency, ring the emergency number, not the GP.
exercise: «In the UK your first stop for most health problems is the GP.» What does GP stand for? | good pupil | *general practitioner | government program | great prize
exercise: «Night cramp in the calf is common; if it happens very often, see a GP.» Where should you go? | To the fire station | *To your family doctor | To a satellite in space | To a big motor race
exercise: In a race report: «The GP was won by a driver from Italy.» What does GP mean here? | Gardening planner | Good, pretty place | *Grand Prix, a big motor race | General practitioner, a family doctor
test: Mia has a bad cough for two weeks. Who should she see first? | *Her GP | A racing driver | A satellite in space
test: What is the best way to check the meaning of a new word? | Guess and never check | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Skip the whole text and stop reading
exam: In «GPS measures the movement every day», what does GPS mean? | A big motor race | A type of medicine | *A satellite system that finds places | A family doctor
